taking on a new client.

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:21.730
Are there ways that
you've found efficiencies

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:25.200
so that you can spin up new
instances of your services

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.340
as a new client comes on?

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.298
CRISTINA FLASCHEN: Yes.

00:04:27.298 --> 00:04:29.130
So Terraform has
been great for us.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:32.460
And the fact that Google
has templates for Terraform

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.370
specifically has made our
deployment process so much more

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.130
straightforward.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:38.310
And again, we're not
reinventing this wheel.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.750
We set this up one time.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.610
We want to focus
on what we do best

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:44.525
and let the folks that
do these things great

00:04:44.525 --> 00:04:46.650
continue to do those things
great while we can take

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:48.000
advantage of that technology.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.170
MAX SALTONSTALL: Looking
back on all the things

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.810
that you have done, are there
any changes you would make

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.820
