that you want to share?

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:54.778
CRISTINA FLASCHEN: Yes.

00:04:54.778 --> 00:04:57.960
So in the very beginning,
we rolled our own Kubernetes

00:04:57.960 --> 00:05:00.720
cluster, did all the management
and maintenance ourselves.

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.220
I think it was a great learning
experience because we really

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:05.150
got deep into the
guts of Kubernetes.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:08.180
But when we learned
that GKE was a thing,

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:10.070
it was a very
obvious choice for us

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:13.130
to migrate from another
cloud provider to Google.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:15.080
And again, it's been
a great experience

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.020
not having to worry about a lot
of the operational and DevOps

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.990
overhead and just relying
on the excellent support

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.040
that we get from Google.

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.810
In addition to that,
we would probably

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:26.160
have gone all in on Stackdriver
a little bit earlier.

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.700
So we were using GCP
and GKE but tried

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:31.370
to use other monitoring
tools and found

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.380
them very cumbersome to set up.

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.630
And they weren't really
